# Addresses: functions about an `ip` (docs/grammar.md "Functions"). An
# `ip` is an IPv4 address, `10.0.0.1`, read from a string where one is
# wanted as an `inet` is. An `iprange` is the addresses between two,
# `10.0.0.10-10.0.0.99`, read the same way.
package ip

#| Whether the address is 0.0.0.0; also a predicate.
#| example: deny "no bind address" where ip.unspecified(a)
fn unspecified(addr: ip) -> bool
